      \field{abstract}{The environmental impact of digital technology has recently been highlighted as a growing concern. In this context, libraries are facing a new challenge: reconciling the general interest objectives assigned to heritage digitization with environmental responsibility. Efficient data management requires the implementation of best practices at every stage of the digitization process, from the capture of images to the design of digital libraries and the digital preservation. The environmental imperative also requires shifting digitization paradigm, as part of a sustainable digital ecosystem that strives for sobriety, without excluding the challenge of societal impact.}
